										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<figure><img width="1024" height="720" src="https://greenpointers.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/SocratesRestaurant_Charlie__Mike_when_it_first_opened_sometime_in_the_mid_to_late_60s-greenpoint-brooklyn-1024x720.png" class="attachment-rss-image-size size-rss-image-size wp-post-image" alt="" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://greenpointers.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/SocratesRestaurant_Charlie__Mike_when_it_first_opened_sometime_in_the_mid_to_late_60s-greenpoint-brooklyn-1024x720.png 1024w, https://greenpointers.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/SocratesRestaurant_Charlie__Mike_when_it_first_opened_sometime_in_the_mid_to_late_60s-greenpoint-brooklyn-300x211.png 300w, https://greenpointers.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/SocratesRestaurant_Charlie__Mike_when_it_first_opened_sometime_in_the_mid_to_late_60s-greenpoint-brooklyn-500x352.png 500w, https://greenpointers.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/SocratesRestaurant_Charlie__Mike_when_it_first_opened_sometime_in_the_mid_to_late_60s-greenpoint-brooklyn-768x540.png 768w, https://greenpointers.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/SocratesRestaurant_Charlie__Mike_when_it_first_opened_sometime_in_the_mid_to_late_60s-greenpoint-brooklyn-400x281.png 400w, https://greenpointers.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/SocratesRestaurant_Charlie__Mike_when_it_first_opened_sometime_in_the_mid_to_late_60s-greenpoint-brooklyn.png 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 34.9rem) calc(100vw - 2rem), (max-width: 53rem) calc(8 * (100vw / 12)), (min-width: 53rem) calc(6 * (100vw / 12)), 100vw"></figure>
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Longtime Greenpointers might remember Socrates Restaurant, an unassuming neighborhood diner at 651 Manhattan Avenue that quietly served the community for decades.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">After immigrating from Cyprus, Charlie and Doula opened Socrates on October 13, 1965, and ran the restaurant with Charlie’s younger brother Mike until retiring and selling it in 2001. Charlie worked the front of the house, greeting regulars and pouring coffee, while Mike served as head chef and Doula was the baker. </p>



